accessWidener v2 official

# Goal lists on vanilla mobs, so a fox can be taught to hunt a creature.
#
# Fabric offers no API for adding a goal to a mob it does not own, and the two ways in are a mixin
# or this. An access widener is the smaller change: it grants exactly two fields and leaves every
# vanilla method body untouched, where a mixin injects into registerGoals and has to be kept working
# across versions and against every other mod injecting into the same place.
#
# The namespace is `official` rather than `named`: Minecraft has shipped unobfuscated since 26.1, so
# there is no separate named namespace left for Loom to remap this through.
#
# 26.2 added a public Mob#getGoalSelector(), so the first line is belt-and-braces — but targetSelector
# still has no accessor, and widening both keeps the two reads symmetrical at the call site.
accessible field net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob goalSelector Lnet/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/GoalSelector;
accessible field net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob targetSelector Lnet/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/GoalSelector;
